<title>GREECE: Intrasoft wins 1.0 bln drs software tender.</title>
<headline>Intrasoft wins 1.0 bln drs software tender.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's software developer and systems integrator Intrasoft signed a software procurement deal worth 1.0 billion drachmas ($4 million) with Malta's Bank of Valletta, it said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Intrasoft won the international tender competing against 14 information technology companies including IBM Denmark, Unisys U.K. and Australia's FNS, it said.</p>
<p>The Bank of Valletta is a commercial bank with a network of 50 branches. ($ = 248.3 Greek Drachmas)</p>
</text>
